# ==========================================
# MUSEUM TICKETING & AI GUIDE
# Environment Configuration File
# ==========================================

# 1. Flask Configuration
# What this is: the key Flask uses to cryptographically sign session cookies
# (so a browser can't forge "I am logged in as user X"). It has nothing to do
# with the database or the Gemini API.
# Do you have to change it to run or evaluate this project? No. The placeholder
# value below works fine for local use — leave it as-is and everything (login,
# booking, the concierge) works normally. It only matters for a real internet-
# facing deployment, where a guessable key would let someone forge a session;
# that does not apply to running the app on your own machine.
# If you want to set a real random one anyway, generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# and paste the output below in place of the placeholder.
# DO NOT commit the actual .env file to version control.
# Note: Double quotes are optional in .env files unless your key has spaces.
# It is generally safer to leave quotes out for API keys.
FLASK_SECRET_KEY=your_super_secret_key_here

# 2. Gemini API Configuration
# Your Google Gemini API Key used for the Cultural Concierge features.
# You can get one from Google AI Studio.
# Note: Do not use quotes around the API key.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest

# 3. Database Configuration
# The raw SQLite database is automatically managed at `instance/app.db` via app.config['DATABASE'].
